# ESPice: ngspice's netlist, with Verilog-A and digital Verilog loaded by
# the netlist itself (Schemify's spec, section 7.2a).
#
# A Verilog-A source is loaded by `.hdl "x.va"`, where ngspice loads the
# OSDI file compiled from it inside a .control block; an N device of it
# says its multiplier `mfactor`. A digital Verilog module is an N device
# too, through VerA's bridges: its pins in the module's port order, every
# bridge parameter the instance gives, then its model; each model a
# `.model <model> <module>` card, each source a `.verilog "x.v"` line
# after the cards, sorted.

base ngspice
drop hdl verilog
---
rule hdl = ".hdl" path
write verilog = name~"N" nodes+ master {...params} -module -file -pins -dirs -code
once verilog master
  .model {master} {module|file.stem}
end
once verilog file
  .verilog "{file}"
end
params device
  m = mfactor
  same ...
end
